<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kutik-Inshushinak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 2100 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/22nd-century-bce">22nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kutik-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inshushinak">Inshushinak</a> (also read Puzur-Inshushinak) was the last king of the Awan dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a>, ruling around 2100 BCE. After the collapse of Akkadian power he freed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a>, brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anshan">Anshan</a> and much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iranian-plateau">Iranian plateau</a> under his rule and campaigned into northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonia">Babylonia</a>, achieving the first genuine unification of the Elamite lands. He promoted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/linear-elamite">Linear Elamite</a> script alongside Akkadian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuneiform">cuneiform</a>, marking a key moment in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a>'s foundation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kutik-inshushinak.jpg" alt="Kutik-Inshushinak" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Darafsh · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_of_Puzur-Inshushinak_with_inscription_in_his_name_(lower_half).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
